# Backend and privacy

These rules apply to any code that sends data off the device, and to work in the
`comaps_backend` repository at `/Users/mo/dev/comaps_backend`.

## Hard invariants

- Raw GPS samples, recorded tracks, exact locations, home or work locations,
  per-pixel visit timestamps, and live movement state are **never** uploaded.
  No build, no flag, no configuration, no debug path.
- The uploaded competition payload is a closed list (product spec §25.2):
  pseudonymous profile identifier, public nickname, area identifier, aggregate
  ownership score, live coverage percentage, eligibility state, weekly
  new-live-pixel count by city, map-data version, score-calculation version,
  last aggregate update time. Nothing else.
- The backend must **reject** anything outside that list at the schema level.
  Documentation is not a control.
- Nothing uploads unless the user has explicitly opted into competition. Consent
  is separate from location permission (spec §20.5, §25.1).
- Uploads are batched and delayed: no more than once per 15 minutes, plus up to
  15 minutes of jitter (spec §25.3). This exists so competition data cannot
  function as a live-location signal. Do not add a "sync now" affordance.
- Sparse-area anonymity is enforced server-side. Where fewer than three
  participants exist in an area, the server does not return nicknames (spec
  §23.4). Client-side hiding is not protection.
- No feature may reveal another user's live location, exact location, presence,
  distance, or last-seen location (spec §25.4).
- Imported GPX data never affects competition, regardless of any flag or
  entitlement state.

## Current baseline

Verify before relying on this; it was true on 2026-07-25.

- The client posts to `{apiBase}/stats/upload`, which **does not exist** in the
  backend.
- `ExploreStatsService` checks for uploads every minute, far more often than the
  specified cadence, and is gated only by a sync flag.
- `IdentityStore` records consent as a boolean with no privacy-policy version and
  no timestamp. Spec §20.5 requires both.
- The backend has only `Explorer` and `Friendship` models, with account and
  friends endpoints under `/api/`. There is no competition, ownership, area, or
  statistics model.
- Friends are a V1 product non-goal (spec §6) but exist in both repositories.
  This is an open question, recorded as OQ-6 in `DECISIONS.md`. Do not resolve it
  unilaterally.

## Backend repository conventions

- Django 5.2 with django-ninja-extra. Settings are split under
  `comaps/settings/`; there is no production settings module yet.
- Auth is `DeviceIdAuth` using `X-Device-Id` and `X-Username` headers.
- There are no tests, no CI, and no linting configuration. Do not assume a test
  command exists. If you add behaviour that needs testing, say that test
  infrastructure is missing rather than claiming coverage.
- V1 deliberately does not build sophisticated anti-cheat. Rate limiting, schema
  validation, and clamping impossible values are the controls, and residual
  cheating risk is accepted.

## When in doubt

If a change would make any payload richer, more frequent, or more precise, stop
and report it. That is a privacy decision, not an implementation detail.
